# use case: keeping a page cache clean.
title Made-up parameters and hosts reach the site but are never stored; the cache keeps only real pages
row  real:box "GET /?page=2" "a real page" | shield:warnbox "request-shield" "cache-query page" | cache:okbox "The page cache" "stores it"
row  junk:box "GET /?x=1, /?x=2 …" "or a made-up host" | nostore:nobox "Answered, not stored" "or 404 for a host"
arrow real -> shield
arrow shield -> cache "cacheable" go
arrow junk -> shield
arrow shield -> nostore "made up"
note A budget for cache misses slows down whoever makes the site render page after page.
